---
name: any-search
description: Research public web pages, verify information from multiple sources, and produce cited summaries or structured research outputs.
Any Search
Use this skill when the user requests research on public websites or information gathering.
Workflow
Clarify the research question, output format, and relevant time period when necessary.
Check which web/search tools and network access are actually available in the current environment. Never claim a tool exists without testing it.
Search using available authorized tools. If no search tool is available, use permitted HTTP requests to public pages when supported; otherwise explain the limitation.
Read primary sources where possible and cross-check important claims.
Record the title, URL, publication/update date if available, and access date for each source.
Return a concise synthesis with source URLs and uncertainty clearly marked.
If requested, export findings as Markdown, CSV, or JSON, preserving attribution.
Guardrails
Respect website terms, robots instructions, licensing, authentication and rate limits.
Do not bypass CAPTCHAs, paywalls, access controls, or anti-bot protections.
Do not collect sensitive personal information or bulk-copy restricted copyrighted content.
If access is blocked, stop and suggest permitted APIs, licensed datasets, or permission from the site owner.
Never invent sources, search results, or tool capabilities.
